…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgAnd Elkanah went to Ramah to his house. And the child did minister unto the LORD before Eli the priest.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@Now the sons of Eli were sons of Belial; they knew not the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»And the priests' custom with the people was, that, when any man offered sacrifice, the priest's servant came, while the flesh was in seething, with a fleshhook of three teeth in his hand;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ½and he struck it into the pan, or kettle, or caldron, or pot; all that the fleshhook brought up the priest took for himself. So they did in Shiloh unto all the Israelites that came thither.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·Also before they burnt the fat, the priest's servant came, and said to the man that sacrificed, Give flesh to roast for the priest; for he will not have sodden flesh of thee, but raw.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙAnd if any man said unto him, Let them not fail to burn the fat presently, and then take as much as thy soul desireth; then he would answer him, Nay; but thou shalt give it me now: and if not, I will take it by force.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmWherefore the sin of the young men was very great before the LORD: for men abhorred the offering of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPBut Samuel ministered before the LORD, being a child, girded with a linen ephod.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•Moreover his mother made him a little coat, and brought it to him from year to year, when she came up with her husband to offer the yearly sacrifice.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And Eli blessed Elkanah and his wife, and said, The LORD give thee seed of this woman for the loan which is lent to the LORD. And they went unto their own home.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…And the LORD visited Hannah, so that she conceived, and bare three sons and two daughters. And the child Samuel grew before the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨Now Eli was very old, and heard all that his sons did unto all Israel; and how they lay with the women that assembled at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd he said unto them, Why do ye such things? for I hear of your evil dealings by all this people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\Nay, my sons; for it is no good report that I hear: ye make the LORD's people to transgress.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙİIf one man sin against another, the judge shall judge him: but if a man sin against the LORD, who shall intreat for him? Notwithstanding they hearkened not unto the voice of their father, because the LORD would slay them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd the child Samuel grew on, and was in favour both with the LORD, and also with men.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬And there came a man of God unto Eli, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Did I plainly appear unto the house of thy father, when they were in Egypt in Pharaoh's house?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙòAnd did I choose him out of all the tribes of Israel to be my priest, to offer upon mine altar, to burn incense, to wear an ephod before me? and did I give unto the house of thy father all the offerings made by fire of the children of Israel?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÔWherefore kick ye at my sacrifice and at mine offering, which I have commanded in my habitation; and honourest thy sons above me, to make yourselves fat with the chiefest of all the offerings of Israel my people?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚWherefore the LORD God of Israel saith, I said indeed that thy house, and the house of thy father, should walk before me for ever: but now the LORD saith, Be it far from me; for them that honour me I will honour, and they that despise me shall be lightly esteemed.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse$¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Behold, the days come, that I will cut off thine arm, and the arm of thy father's house, that there shall not be an old man in thine house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And thou shalt see an enemy in my habitation, in all the wealth which God shall give Israel: and there shall not be an old man in thine house for ever.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄAnd the man of thine, whom I shall not cut off from mine altar, shall be to consume thine eyes, and to grieve thine heart: and all the increase of thine house shall die in the flower of their age.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And this shall be a sign unto thee, that shall come upon thy two sons, on Hophni and Phinehas; in one day they shall die both of them.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄAnd I will raise me up a faithful priest, that shall do according to that which is in mine heart and in my mind: and I will build him a sure house; and he shall walk before mine anointed for ever.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙöAnd it shall come to pass, that every one that is left in thine house shall come and crouch to him for a piece of silver and a morsel of bread, and shall say, Put me, I pray thee, into one of the priests' offices, that I may eat a piece of bread.¦layout ªlast_verse$